Subject: [PATCH] stmmac: honor caller gfp flags for RX buffer allocation

RX buffers were always allocated with GFP_ATOMIC, which fails when the free
lists are empty even though reclaimable memory exists. The open path passes
GFP_KERNEL, so use the caller flags to allow reclaim during ring setup.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c	2026-10-27 19:51:04.600261154 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c	2026-10-27 19:51:09.048278803 +0000
@@ -1657,7 +1657,7 @@
 {
 	struct stmmac_rx_queue *rx_q = &dma_conf->rx_queue[queue];
 	struct stmmac_rx_buffer *buf = &rx_q->buf_pool[i];
-	gfp_t gfp = (GFP_ATOMIC | __GFP_NOWARN);
+	gfp_t gfp = flags | __GFP_NOWARN;
 
 	if (priv->dma_cap.host_dma_width <= 32)
 		gfp |= GFP_DMA32;
